/Gshoe2006/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Gshoe2006/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Gshoe2006/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Gshoe2006/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Gshoe2006/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "content_type": "application/octet-stream", "state": "uploaded", "size": 193486, "digest": "sha256:a15dc2f235409a226228fffca3007ed62164294064b79ac5646421b39679ff5a", "download_count": 0, "created_at": "2026-11-19T00:19:20Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-19T00:19:21Z", "browser_download_url": "https://github.com/Gshoe2006/inkline/releases/download/3.1.0/inkline-3.1.0.run"}], "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Gshoe2006/inkline/tarball/3.1.0", "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Gshoe2006/inkline/zipball/3.1.0", "body_html": "<h1>Inkline 3.1.0</h1>\n<p>Inkline 3.1 lets you take back changes and get back to photos you've used before.</p>\n<h2>What's new</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Undo and Redo.</strong> The new <strong>Edit</strong> menu has Undo (Ctrl+Z) and Redo (Ctrl+Shift+Z). They cover every change to a design: settings, New design, presets, switching between Make and Convert, crops, and adding, moving or removing photos. The menu names what it will undo, such as \"Undo Line weight\" or \"Undo \u201cMaze booklet with answers\u201d\".\n<ul>\n<li>A whole slider drag, or typing in one field, is one step, so a single Undo takes it all back.</li>\n<li>Each click is its own step.</li>\n<li>Turning pages, choosing a photo to crop, saving and printing aren't changes, so they don't add steps.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Undo history.</strong> <strong>Edit \u2192 History\u2026</strong> (Ctrl+H) opens a list of every step. Click any step to go straight back, or forward, to that point. The top row, \"Start\", is how things were before your first change.</li>\n<li><strong>Recent photos.</strong> <strong>File \u2192 Open recent</strong> lists the last 10 photos you opened, newest first, and keeps them between runs. Hover over one to see where it is on disk, and choose one to open it again. If a photo has been moved or deleted, Inkline says so and takes it off the list. <strong>Clear list</strong> empties it.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Good to know</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The undo history lasts for one session.</strong> It starts fresh each time you open Inkline. Your settings and designs are still restored as before.</li>\n<li><strong>Text fields keep their own Ctrl+Z</strong> while you're typing in them.</li>\n<li><strong>The recent list is saved in <code>~/.config/inkline/recent.json</code>,</strong> next to your presets.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrading</h2>\n<p>Nothing changes in what Inkline needs: Python 3 with PySide6 and numpy, as in 3.0. Your presets and settings carry over.</p>\n<p><strong>Arch / CachyOS / Manjaro</strong></p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"sudo pacman -U inkline-3.1.0-1-any.pkg.tar.zst\"><pre>sudo pacman -U inkline-3.1.0-1-any.pkg.tar.zst</pre></div>\n<p><strong>Any other distro</strong></p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"sh inkline-3.1.0.run            # or --system for every user\"><pre>sh inkline-3.1.0.run            <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> or --system for every user</span></pre></div>\n<h2>Found a problem?</h2>\n<p>Please open an issue saying what you did, what you expected, and what happened. Include your distro, and the printer if it's about printing.</p>"}]